{"node":{"id":"HP:0030466","label":"Abnormal full-field electroretinogram","ic":5.273,"definition":"An anomaly observed by full-field electroretinogram (ffERG). The ffERG measures the light-induced electrical activity of the retina at the corneal surface. Specifically, the ffERG records the global or total retinal electrical response to a full-field (Ganzfield) light stimulus. Isolation of the rod and cone components has important diagnostic value in differentiating between various retinal diseases. Modifying the properties of the light-stimulus (wavelength, strength, and flicker rate) as well as the adaptive state of the retina can separate the rod and cone functions of the ffERG."},"diseases":[{"id":"MONDO:0010674","label":"mucopolysaccharidosis type 2","in_core":true,"edge":{"id":"e_32039b0de8e1","source":"MONDO:0010674","target":"HP:0030466","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:580 · ORPHA:580","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/580","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.3,"snippet":"Mucopolysaccharidosis type 2: Abnormal full-field electroretinogram (frequency HP:0040283) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:580","level":"curated","date":"2026-06-23","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/580","confidence":0.3,"snippet":"Abnormal full-field electroretinogram — Occasional (29-5%)"}],"contradicting":[],"confidence":0.3,"independent_sources":["Orphanet"],"level":"curated"},"confidence":0.3},{"id":"MONDO:0015993","label":"cone-rod dystrophy","in_core":false,"edge":{"id":"e_b2925e363307","source":"MONDO:0015993","target":"HP:0030466","type":"has_phenotype","evidence":[{"db":"HPO","origin":"Orphanet","record":"ORPHA:1872 · ORPHA:1872","url":"https://www.orpha.net/en/disease/detail/1872","level":"curated","date":"2026-09-02","confidence":0.6,"snippet":"Cone rod dystrophy: Abnormal full-field electroretinogram (frequency HP:0040282) [TAS]"},{"db":"Orphanet","origin"